  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Exodus",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 10,
    "summary": "The Lord sends a plague of locusts—This is followed by thick darkness in all Egypt for three days—Moses is cast out from the presence of Pharaoh.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And the Lord said unto Moses, Go in unto Pharaoh: for I have hardened his heart, and the heart of his servants, that I might shew these my signs before him:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 53,
            "text": "JST Ex. 10:1 … for he hath hardened his heart, and the hearts of his servants, therefore I will show these my signs before him;"
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Exodus 10:1",
        "book": "Exodus",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And that thou mayest tell in the ears of thy son, and of thy son’s son, what things I have wrought in Egypt, and my signs which I have done among them; that ye may know how that I am the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "D&C 93:42 (42–43); Moses 6:58."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 180,
            "end": 182
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Exodus 10:2",
        "book": "Exodus",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And Moses and Aaron came in unto Pharaoh, and said unto him, Thus saith the Lord God of the Hebrews, How long wilt thou refuse to humble thyself before me? let my people go, that they may serve me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 130,
            "end": 136,
            "text": "Ex. 5:2; 9:17. TG Submissiveness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Exodus 10:3",
        "book": "Exodus",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Else, if thou refuse to let my people go, behold, to morrow will I bring the locusts into thy coast:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 84,
            "text": "Ps. 105:34; Mosiah 12:6 (6–7). TG Plague."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Exodus 10:4",
        "book": "Exodus",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And they shall cover the face of the earth, that one cannot be able to see the earth: and they shall eat the residue of that which is escaped, which remaineth unto you from the hail, and shall eat every tree which groweth for you out of the field:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 109,
            "end": 116,
            "text": "Ex. 9:32 (31–32)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Exodus 10:5",
        "book": "Exodus",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And they shall fill thy houses, and the houses of all thy servants, and the houses of all the Egyptians; which neither thy fathers, nor thy fathers’ fathers have seen, since the day that they were upon the earth unto this day. And he turned himself, and went out from Pharaoh.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Exodus 10:6",
        "book": "Exodus",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And Pharaoh’s servants said unto him, How long shall this man be a snare unto us? let the men go, that they may serve the Lord their God: knowest thou not yet that Egypt is destroyed?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "2 Ne. 18:14; Mosiah 7:29."
          },
          {
            "start": 173,
            "end": 182,
            "text": "OR ruined."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
